# Auth / password-reset / set-username — review follow-ups

From code review of uncommitted auth work (#220 / #335). Codegen items withdrawn — generated files are gitignored and verified on disk.

**Merge readiness:** needs work

---

## Blockers (before merge)

- [x] **Restore registration bloc tests** — `packages/core/test/src/application/registration/registration_bloc_test.dart` lost ~10 cases (signup validation, sign-in errors, prefill, cancel, etc.). Restore deleted coverage; add tests for `resolveEmailForLogin` returning null and `needsUsernameSetup` on Google sign-in.

- [ ] **i18n: map new core error strings** — Hardcoded English in core is not wired in `apps/multichoice/lib/i18n/localize_core_message.dart`. Add keys to `en.i18n.json` / `nl.i18n.json` and switch cases for e.g. `No account found for this username.`, password success messages, invalid reset link, reauth-before-change messages. Run `make slang`.

- [ ] **PROD App Links** — `firebase/public/.well-known/assetlinks.json` only lists `co.za.zanderkotze.multichoice.dev`. Add prod package `co.za.zanderkotze.multichoice` + release SHA-256, or separate Hosting deploy per Firebase project (see `docs/password-reset-deep-links.md`).

- [ ] **Flavor-specific deep-link hosts** — `AndroidManifest.xml` declares both DEV and PROD `firebaseapp.com` hosts in one manifest while `assetlinks.json` only verifies DEV. Use flavor manifest overlays so each build matches its Hosting `assetlinks.json`.

- [ ] **Run validation** — `melos test:core`, `melos exec --scope=multichoice -- flutter analyze` after test/i18n fixes.

---

## Should fix (same PR or immediate follow-up)

- [ ] **Username login limitation** — `LoginService.resolveEmailForLogin` reads username→email from local secure storage only; fails on new device/reinstall. Document as MVP in user-facing copy/docs, or persist mapping server-side before shipping username login UX.

- [ ] **Username setup confirmation** — `isUsernameConfirmed` / `markUsernameConfirmed` are per-device, not per Firebase user. Google users may be re-prompted on every new device. Persist in Firebase (custom claim, Firestore user doc, or authoritative `displayName`).

- [x] **Set-username tests** — Add `SetUsernameBloc` tests (mirror `reset_password_bloc_test.dart`). Consider blocking home navigation until username is set, or re-prompt on next launch.

- [x] **Reset-password bloc tests** — Add coverage for `isSetPassword: true` (`linkPassword`) and reauth failure paths.

- [ ] **Profile password row flash** — `ProfileState.initial()` defaults `hasPasswordProvider` to `true`; Google-only users may briefly see “Update Password”. Default to `false` or hide until `ProfileLoadStarted` completes.

- [ ] **Server-side username uniqueness** — `RegistrationService.setUsername` only updates Firebase `displayName`; no uniqueness check. Add Firestore/Cloud Function check before `updateDisplayName`.

- [ ] **Firebase Hosting landing page** — `firebase/public/index.html` is default boilerplate with `useEmulator=true`. Replace with minimal landing page or remove; set `useEmulator=false` for production.

- [ ] **iOS deep links** — No Universal Links / associated-domains in diff. Document as Android-only for this release, or add iOS entitlements before claiming cross-platform deep links.

